-- The third BPMN fixture, and the only one that draws a CONVERGING parallel
-- gateway. It exists because without it nothing a user could actually write
-- demonstrates a conjunction: `offering.l4` and `handover.l4` both decline, for
-- two different and correct reasons, so a regression that stopped this exporter
-- drawing joins altogether would have left every golden unchanged.
--
-- What makes it joinable is narrow, and worth stating because the boundary is
-- much tighter than it looks (see "the boundary of what can be joined" in
-- jl4/tests/BpmnExport.hs):
--
--   * every branch is a PERMISSION. An obligation would not do: L4 gives every
--     MUST a LEST to BREACH whether the drafter writes one or not, so an
--     obligation branch stops at two places, and a converging parallel gateway
--     needs all its branches to stop at the same one.
--   * no branch carries a WITHIN. A deadline on a permission becomes a lapse
--     timer, which is a second and mutually exclusive way for that branch to
--     arrive at the join — and a parallel gateway would then wait for both.
--   * no PROVIDED guard, which would put a condition on an incoming flow of a
--     parallel gateway. That is a spec violation outright.
--
-- So: DO NOT add a deadline to this file to make it more realistic. Doing so
-- silently converts the suite's only positive join case into a fourth negative
-- one. That is not hypothetical — it is exactly what happened to `handover.l4`,
-- whose header used to advertise its RAND as the join exhibit.
--
-- A branch may still be a chain, as the Resident's is: what the proof needs is
-- one unconditional arrival per branch, not one task per branch.
--
-- Fixture for `jl4/tests/BpmnExport.hs`.

DECLARE Participant IS ONE OF Resident, Developer, Registrar

DECLARE Submission IS ONE OF
  `file written comments`
  `file a response`
  `publish the record`

`the consultation` MEANS
      (PARTY Resident MAY `file written comments`
         HENCE PARTY Registrar MAY `publish the record`)
  RAND (PARTY Developer MAY `file a response`)
